From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: a logit gather broadcasts one block a rank, not one a row

Our fork `ai-engine` at 0a77dcd7d, "glm cuda: a logit gather broadcasts one block a
rank, so TP=3 prompt_logprobs past ~100 tokens no longer hangs" (its own "Fixes #1559").
The fork diff applies to our tree unchanged for the three source files, so these are its
lines.

Sampler.gather copied this rank's columns into `full` row by row and then queued one
ncclBroadcast per row per rank inside one NCCL group. At TP=3 a 128-row prompt-logprob
pass posts 381 broadcasts in one group and never leaves ncclGroupEnd, so the pass hangs.
Each rank's columns are already one packed [rows][span] block, so the fork broadcasts
that block once a rank into a new `stage` buffer and places each block into its columns
of `full` with one cuMemcpy2DAsync. The bytes in `full` are the same; the number of
broadcasts a gather is now the world, whatever the rows.

Three call sites take the new `stage` argument: Sampler.draw, prompt_logprobs.run (where
the pass's own 128-row Buffers gain a `stage` of the same size as `full`) and
structured.drawWhole.

This completes no patch of ours. The pin has the identical row-by-row Spread.post
(work/pin/tree/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_sampler.zig), and all three source files here
are byte-identical to the pin before this patch, so it is a fork fix we had never taken,
not a port regression.

Left out of the fork's commit: nothing from the three source files. Added beyond it, in
zig/glm_prompt_logprobs_host.zig (patch 0024 owns that file here):

  - the `copy2d` no-op and `d.api.cuMemcpy2DAsync_v2 = copy2d` in Heads.score. Heads
    builds its driver from `undefined` and sets only the entry points the code under
    test calls, so without the stub the two tests that reach `score` call a garbage
    function pointer. The fork added the same stub in its later 03138041e; the comment
    here states what the code does rather than naming that commit.
  - `e.smp.stage`, beside the `e.smp.full` the test already sets. The fork leaves the
    new field undefined in its host test; our `run` reads it on the window path that
    these tests take, so we give it an address.

One place this patch goes beyond the fork's own edit: `Sampler.copy`, the 1D
device-to-device helper, is removed. `gather` was its only caller in either tree and it is
private, so after this change nothing can reach it; the fork leaves it in place and a dead
private helper is not worth carrying.

Gates: zig build test-glm-logprobs-host passes (7/7) with this patch, and patch 08 of this
lane makes that step part of test-cuda-host, which it was not before.

What a GPU run must show: a TP=3 serve answering a prompt_logprobs request over 128
tokens at all (the hang this fixes), and the same logprob words as TP=1 for the same
prompt. The bf16 bytes `full` holds should be identical to the old path, so a digest of
a structured or sampled decode on three ranks is the cheap check that `place` and the
broadcast layout agree.

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat (work/reseat/DECISIONS.md):
- v1.2.7 has the same row-by-row Spread.post (cuda_sampler.zig unchanged in 9c9bf542..v1.2.7); applies as is.
- source: work/fold/0001-logit-gather-blocks.patch

